## What you get

| Feature | How it works |
|---|---|
| **Glass body** | Fresnel term creates the characteristic bright edge / dark center look of a transparent sphere |
| **Swirl pattern** | 5-octave FBM noise, gently rotated over time, blended into a cool blue → warm amber palette |
| **Subsurface glow** | A fake SSS lobe (`sss`) that lets light appear to pass through the marble |
| **Specular highlights** | Two Blinn-Phong speculars (tight + broad) for a crisp white hot-spot plus soft bloom |
| **Rim glow** | Fresnel multiplied by a cool tint adds the tell-tale glass edge highlight |
| **Tone mapping** | Reinhard + gamma correction keeps everything visible and cinematic |

